      <section class="doc-section" id="quick-start">
        <h2 class="section-title">Getting Started — Quick Start</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Follow these four steps to go live quickly and safely.</p>

        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">1</div>
            <div>
              <h4>Create Your Account</h4>
              <p>Sign up at zenopay.in and complete KYC verification to enable merchant features.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">2</div>
            <div>
              <h4>Get Your API Keys</h4>
              <p>Navigate to Dashboard &gt; API Keys and generate test/live key pairs for your app.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">3</div>
            <div>
              <h4>Install the SDK</h4>
              <p>Install official SDK in your server environment.</p>
              <div class="code-block"><pre class="code-content">npm install zenopay-node</pre></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">4</div>
            <div>
              <h4>Make Your First Payment</h4>
              <p>Call the create payment endpoint and redirect users to hosted checkout.</p>
              <div class="code-block"><pre class="code-content">POST /v2/payments
{
  "amount": 5000,
  "currency": "INR"
}</pre></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section class="doc-section" id="authentication">
        <h2 class="section-title">Authentication</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Secure your integration with API keys and verify webhook signatures via HMAC.</p>

        <div class="table-wrap" style="padding:28px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;">API Key Authentication</h3>
          <div class="info-box">Recommended for server-side integrations only. Never expose API keys in client-side code.</div>
          <div class="code-block"><pre class="code-content">Authorization: Bearer sk_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxx</pre></div>

          <h3>HMAC Webhook Signature</h3>
          <div class="code-block"><pre class="code-content">const expected = crypto
  .createHmac('sha256', webhookSecret)
  .update(rawBody)
  .digest('hex');

if (expected !== signature) throw new Error('Invalid signature');</pre></div>

          <h3 class="table-title" style="margin-top:16px;">Key Types</h3>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Key Type</th><th>Prefix</th><th>Environment</th><th>Usage</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Live Secret Key</td><td><code>sk_live_</code></td><td>Production</td><td>Server-side only</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Test Secret Key</td><td><code>sk_test_</code></td><td>Sandbox</td><td>Development</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Live Public Key</td><td><code>pk_live_</code></td><td>Production</td><td>Client-side safe</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Test Public Key</td><td><code>pk_test_</code></td><td>Sandbox</td><td>Development</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="warning"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><span>Never share your secret API key. Do not include it in frontend code, version control, or public repositories.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section class="doc-section" id="errors">
        <h2 class="section-title">Error Codes Reference</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">ZenoPay uses standard HTTP status codes. All error responses return <code>error_code</code>, <code>message</code>, and <code>details</code>.</p>

        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>HTTP Code</th><th>Error Code</th><th>Message</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="error-section-row"><td colspan="4">4XX Client Errors</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="http-badge http-400">400</span></td><td><code style="color:#3B82F6;">INVALID_AMOUNT</code></td><td style="color:#475569;">Amount must be greater than zero.</td><td style="color:#94A3B8;">Provided amount is malformed or too low.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="http-badge http-401">401</span></td><td><code style="color:#3B82F6;">AUTH_FAILED</code></td><td style="color:#475569;">Invalid API key.</td><td style="color:#94A3B8;">Missing/incorrect bearer token.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="http-badge http-422">422</span></td><td><code style="color:#3B82F6;">VALIDATION_ERROR</code></td><td style="color:#475569;">Request validation failed.</td><td style="color:#94A3B8;">Field-level input errors.</td></tr>
              <tr class="error-section-row"><td colspan="4">5XX Server Errors</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="http-badge http-500">500</span></td><td><code style="color:#3B82F6;">INTERNAL_ERROR</code></td><td style="color:#475569;">Unexpected server error.</td><td style="color:#94A3B8;">Please retry or contact support.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section class="doc-section" id="webhooks-overview">
        <h2 class="section-title">Webhooks Overview</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Subscribe to events and process asynchronous notifications for payments, refunds, transfers, and user updates.</p>

        <div class="events-grid" id="webhook-events">
          <article class="event-card">
            <div class="event-head"><div class="event-icon"><i class="fas fa-exchange-alt"></i></div><div class="event-meta"><h4>Payment Events</h4><span>6 events</span></div></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.created</code><p>When payment intent is created.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.completed</code><p>When payment is successful.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.failed</code><p>When payment attempt fails.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.cancelled</code><p>When payment is cancelled.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.refunded</code><p>When full/partial refund settles.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>payment.expired</code><p>When payment expires.</p></div>
          </article>

          <article class="event-card">
            <div class="event-head"><div class="event-icon"><i class="fas fa-undo"></i></div><div class="event-meta"><h4>Refund Events</h4><span>3 events</span></div></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>refund.created</code><p>Refund requested.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>refund.processed</code><p>Refund completed.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>refund.failed</code><p>Refund could not be processed.</p></div>
          </article>

          <article class="event-card">
            <div class="event-head"><div class="event-icon"><i class="fas fa-paper-plane"></i></div><div class="event-meta"><h4>Transfer Events</h4><span>3 events</span></div></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>transfer.created</code><p>Transfer initiated.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>transfer.completed</code><p>Transfer settled.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>transfer.failed</code><p>Transfer failed.</p></div>
          </article>

          <article class="event-card">
            <div class="event-head"><div class="event-icon"><i class="fas fa-user"></i></div><div class="event-meta"><h4>User Events</h4><span>3 events</span></div></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>user.created</code><p>User account created.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>user.verified</code><p>User KYC verified.</p></div>
            <div class="event-item"><code>user.suspended</code><p>User account suspended.</p></div>
          </article>
